{"jobs":[{"job":"debit_card_decline_diagnosis","into":["debit_card_decline_diagnosis"],"aliases":["debit card declined with no code shown, card active, recent client check deposit not yet available"],"kept":{"steps":["ask_identity","lookup_user","check_identity","get_time_verif","log_verif","ask_decline_details","unlock_accounts","get_accounts","unlock_cards","get_cards","unlock_txns","get_txns","route_by_code","unfreeze","check_account_status","check_fraud_alert","clear_fraud_alert","bank_alert_transfer","check_velocity","clear_velocity","check_expired","check_limit","check_balance","offer_options","transfer_funds","transfer_error","overdraft_note","transfer_if_error","next_issue"],"rules":["Verify identity with 2 of DOB, email, phone or address","Code 05 / unknown decline: check card status","If the account status is SUSPENDED or RESTRICTED","Only a customer_initiated fraud alert can be cleared","A velocity block may be lifted early","Never tell the customer that a card is fraud-flagged","Do not claim the card is broken or frozen","A card can be unfrozen only if it is FROZEN","Bank-initiated alerts cannot be cleared","Deposited funds: standard deposits","A temporary limit increase needs","Only one temporary increase per card in 24 hours.","A transfer between the customer's accounts needs","Security transfers use the Tier 1 reason"]},"edits":[{"op":"add","list":"aliases","item":"debit card declined with no code shown, card active, recent client check deposit not yet available","why":"This customer saw no code, the card was ACTIVE, and the cause was a recently deposited check that was not yet fully available."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"check_card_status","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"FROZEN: ask whether to unfreeze","quote":"If status is FROZEN → Ask customer if they want to unfreeze. If yes, follow the freezing/unfreezing card protocol.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003"},{"clause":"CLOSED: no longer active, look for another active card or offer a replacement","quote":"If status is CLOSED → Inform customer this card is no longer active. Check if they have another active card or offer to order a replacement.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003"},{"clause":"PENDING: not activated yet, activation protocol","quote":"If status is PENDING → Card not yet activated. Follow protocol to activate it.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003"},{"clause":"ACTIVE: continue","quote":"If status is ACTIVE → Continue to step 2.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_003"}]},"why":"Kept as written. The step has four status branches under one quote, so each now has its own basis quote (reading rule 19)."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"security_codes","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"never say the card is flagged for fraud","quote":"tell the customer their card has been flagged for fraud over the phone.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"},{"clause":"say transactions cannot be processed, visit a branch with ID; transfer only if pressed","quote":"Say: 'I'm sorry, but I'm unable to process transactions on this card. For assistance, please visit a Rho-Bank branch with valid ID.' Use transfer_to_human_agents if customer presses for details.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"},{"clause":"suspected-fraud codes get the same non-disclosure","quote":"Say: 'There's a security matter affecting your card that requires in-person verification. Please visit a branch with your ID.' Do NOT attempt to clear or explain.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"},{"clause":"card reported stolen goes to its own protocol","quote":"Card was reported stolen. This code requires EXTRA CAUTION.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"},{"clause":"reported lost: ask whether they reported it","quote":"Check if customer actually reported it: 'I see this card was reported lost. Did you report it lost?'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"}]},"why":"Kept. Added one basis quote for each deciding clause."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"request_limit_increase","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"all eligibility checks before granting","quote":"Before granting a temporary limit increase, verify ALL of the following:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"account OPEN","quote":"The linked checking account must be OPEN (in good standing)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"at least 60 days old","quote":"The account must be at least 60 days old","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"no overdraft fee in 30 days","quote":"No overdraft fees in the last 30 days","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"card ACTIVE","quote":"The debit card must be ACTIVE","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"once per 24 hours","quote":"Only one temporary increase per 24-hour period per card","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"at most 150%","quote":"New limit cannot exceed 150% of current limit (50% boost maximum)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"limit_type atm or purchase","quote":"limit_type: 'atm' or 'purchase'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_040"},{"clause":"only if the customer accepts the offer","quote":"Tell customer: 'I can request a temporary increase that lasts 24 hours. Would you like me to do that?'","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_005"},{"clause":"not a Light Green Account (parental controls)","quote":"If account_class is 'Light Green Account', there may be parental controls.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_005"},{"clause":"Light Green controls are not changed without the guardian","quote":"Do NOT modify parental controls without the guardian's authorization.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_light_green_account_005"}]},"why":"Kept. Each eligibility clause now has its own basis quote."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"explain_insufficient","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"tell the customer their balance","quote":"Inform customer of their balance.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"pending items and checks reduce available funds","quote":"Pending card transactions and checks can decrease available funds before they appear as posted.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"standard deposits typically available in 1-2 business days","quote":"Standard deposits are typically available within 1-2 business days.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"},{"clause":"extended review; date shown in the app","quote":"Certain deposits may be subject to extended review. You will see the expected availability date in the app after submission.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"}]},"why":"Kept. The deposit timing clauses come from doc 011, so they now have their own basis quotes."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"explain_availability","fields":{"do":"Tell the customer that funds from a recently deposited check may not all be available yet. Availability depends on the account type and the deposit amount. Standard deposits are typically available within 1-2 business days, some deposits get extended review, and the app shows the expected availability date. Read the deposit from get_txns (check_deposit or mobile_deposit, posted or pending), not from a date you assume. Do not tell the customer the card is broken or frozen.","basis":[{"clause":"availability depends on account type and amount","quote":"Availability depends on your account type and the deposit amount.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"},{"clause":"1-2 business days","quote":"Standard deposits are typically available within 1-2 business days.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"},{"clause":"extended review, date in app","quote":"Certain deposits may be subject to extended review. You will see the expected availability date in the app after submission.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"},{"clause":"deposit types in the transaction record","quote":"Transaction status, either 'posted' or 'pending'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_018"}]},"why":"The old wording ('Give the deposit availability timeline') did not say which timeline. It now states the doc 011 figures and the record they are read from. This customer asks how long the check takes to clear.","quote":"Standard deposits are typically available within 1-2 business days.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_011"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"no_faster_access","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"transfer from another account or add funds","quote":"Add funds or transfer money from another account to restore a positive available balance.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"smaller purchase","quote":"Offer options: 'Would you like to transfer funds from another account, or would you prefer to make a smaller transaction?'","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"no documented early release of deposited funds","source":"none","why":"Searched 'check hold', 'clear', 'funds availability' and 'deposit hold' across the KB. Docs 011, 004 and 006 give timing only. No document gives an action or tool that releases a deposit early."}]},"why":"Kept. Added basis. Nothing in the documents supports early release, so that clause is marked source none."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"auth_holds","fields":{"basis":[{"clause":"ask about recent authorization holds","quote":"Ask the customer if they have any recent authorization holds that might be reducing their available balance.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"common sources","quote":"Common sources: gas stations (often $75-$150 pre-auth), hotels, car rentals, restaurants (tip buffer).","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"holds release in 1-3 business days","quote":"These holds typically release in 1-3 business days.","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"},{"clause":"name the pending debits","quote":"Explain: 'You have pending transactions totaling $[amount] that haven't posted yet.'","doc":"doc_checking_accounts_checking_accounts_(general)_006"}]},"why":"Kept. Added one basis quote for each clause."}]},{"job":"chip_cvv_mismatch_card_review","into":["chip_cvv_mismatch_card_review"],"aliases":["chip keeps failing on an undamaged card; transaction review finds an out-of-state charge the customer denies"],"kept":{"steps":["ensure_verified","get_accounts_82","ask_damage","damaged_replace","get_cards_82","review_txns","classify_review","freeze_undamaged","time_for_dispute","check_prefiling_82","unlock_dispute","unlock_close","explain_close","ask_replacement","unlock_order","confirm_order","action_error_82"],"rules":["An undamaged card with chip/CVV errors is a possible clone","Use fraud categories when fraud is suspected","Fraud categories map to close_and_reissue.","Provisional credit is required when the report is timely","Fraud/lost/stolen closures skip the 14-day","Entry tier: 48h wait after closure","Evergreen Account is Premium tier.","Dispute open-count limits per account","Only an ACTIVE card can be frozen.","A card with pending transactions cannot be closed until they settle."]},"edits":[{"op":"add","list":"aliases","item":"chip keeps failing on an undamaged card; transaction review finds an out-of-state charge the customer denies","why":"This customer's case: a repeated chip error with no code on an undamaged card. The review found an in-store charge in another state that the customer says she did not make."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"liability_notice","fields":{"do":"Before filing, tell the customer their Regulation E liability exposure. Doc 031 counts it from the statement showing the transaction: reported within 2 business days of that statement, maximum $50; within 60 days, maximum $500; after 60 days, unlimited liability.","basis":[{"clause":"inform before filing","quote":"Before proceeding, inform the customer of their liability exposure based on when they noticed the unauthorized activity:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"$50 tier","quote":"Reported within 2 business days of statement: Maximum liability $50","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"$500 tier","quote":"Reported within 60 days of statement: Maximum liability $500","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"unlimited after 60 days","quote":"Reported after 60 days: Unlimited liability - customer may not recover funds","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"Regulation E limits liability by reporting speed","quote":"If someone uses your debit card without permission, your liability is limited based on how quickly you report it:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_037"}]},"why":"The step now names the event each tier counts from (the statement), per doc 031. It also cites the Regulation E document that the dispute tool's description names (D16).","quote":"Reported within 60 days of statement: Maximum liability $500","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"gather_dispute_info","fields":{"do":"For each denied transaction, ask one question at a time:
- whether the customer still has the physical card;
- whether their PIN may have been compromised (yes_shared, yes_observed, no, unknown);
- when they first noticed the charge;
- how the charge was made, if the record and the customer's account do not show it (in store with PIN or signature, or online/phone);
- whether they contacted the merchant;
- whether they agree that this conversation serves as their written statement.
For a fraud dispute over $500, ask whether they filed a police report, and recommend one if not.","basis":[{"clause":"card in possession","quote":"Do you still have your physical debit card in your possession?","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"PIN compromised","quote":"Do you believe your PIN may have been compromised?","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"discovery date","quote":"Date customer first noticed the issue.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"transaction type from circumstances","quote":"Determine from user circumstances.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"merchant contact","quote":"Have you attempted to resolve this directly with the merchant?","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"written statement","quote":"We can use this conversation as your written statement if you agree.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"police report over $500","quote":"For fraud disputes over $500, ask if customer has filed a police report. If not, recommend they do so.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]},"why":"file_dispute needs discovery_date, transaction_type and contacted_merchant from the customer, and the old step did not ask for them. Doc 031 lists each one."},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"file_dispute","fields":{"if":"the customer denies a transaction, says they want it disputed, and it passed check_prefiling_82","args":{"agent_tool_name":"file_debit_card_transaction_dispute_6281","arguments":{"transaction_id":"the denied transaction's id from review_txns","account_id":"the checking account from get_accounts_82","card_id":"the card's card_id from get_cards_82","user_id":"the verified user","dispute_category":"card_present_fraud for an in-store/physical charge; card_not_present_fraud for an online/phone charge","transaction_date":"the record's date, MM/DD/YYYY","discovery_date":"the date the customer first noticed it, MM/DD/YYYY (the get_current_time date from time_for_dispute if they first noticed it in this conversation)","disputed_amount":"the absolute value of the recorded amount","transaction_type":"pin_purchase or signature_purchase for an in-store charge, online_purchase for online/phone, from the record and the customer's answer","card_in_possession":"the customer's answer (boolean)","pin_compromised":"yes_shared, yes_observed, no or unknown, from the customer","contacted_merchant":"the customer's answer (boolean)","police_report_filed":"the customer's answer (boolean)","written_statement_provided":"true if the customer agreed","provisional_credit_eligible":"true when all four REQUIRED conditions of doc 032 hold (filing_a_debit_card_transaction_dispute decide_provisional_credit), otherwise false","customer_max_liability_amount":"the liability_notice tier's own figure: 50, 500, or -1 after 60 days","card_action":"close_and_reissue"}},"basis":[{"clause":"fraud with the card physically present","quote":"'card_present_fraud': Physical card used fraudulently (not by customer) - USE THIS when fraud suspected and card was physically present","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"online or phone fraud","quote":"'card_not_present_fraud': Online/phone transaction customer didn't make - USE THIS when fraud suspected for online/phone transactions","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"card_action close_and_reissue","quote":"'card_present_fraud' → 'close_and_reissue'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"provisional credit per guidelines","quote":"Provisional Credit is REQUIRED when ALL of these conditions are met:","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_032"},{"clause":"liability tier figure","quote":"Reported within 60 days of statement: Maximum liability $500","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"discovery date is when first noticed","quote":"Date customer first noticed the issue.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"in-store PIN purchase","quote":"'pin_purchase': In-store purchase with PIN","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"in-store signature purchase","quote":"'signature_purchase': In-store purchase with signature","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]},"why":"D9: the old args left out customer_max_liability_amount, which the tool requires. The old args also fixed discovery_date to 'today', but doc 031 defines it as the date the customer first noticed the issue. The liability figure is the tier's own figure (reading rule 14), as in closing_cancelling_a_debit_card.","quote":"Date customer first noticed the issue.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"check_close_82","fields":{"do":"Before closing, check four things:
1. The card belongs to the verified user.
2. Its status in get_cards_82 is ACTIVE or PENDING. If it is FROZEN, unfreeze_before_close_82 runs once checks 1, 3 and 4 pass. If it is CLOSED, it needs no closure.
3. review_txns shows no pending transactions.
4. There is no pending refund, unless the customer acknowledges in writing that it will be credited to the linked checking account.
The 14-day card age does not apply to fraud_suspected. If check 1, 3 or 4 fails, tell the customer what must be resolved and do not close.","basis":[{"clause":"owner","quote":"Customer must be the owner of the debit card (verify user_id matches)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"ACTIVE or PENDING","quote":"The debit card must currently be in ACTIVE or PENDING status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"no pending transactions","quote":"No pending transactions: The card must not have any pending or processing transactions.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"pending refund or written acknowledgement","quote":"If pending refunds exist, inform the customer they must wait for the refunds to process (typically 3-5 business days) or acknowledge in writing that the refunds will be credited to the linked checking account instead.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"age bypass","quote":"These reasons bypass the minimum card age requirement (requirement 6) for security purposes","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"stop and explain","quote":"If any requirement is not met, inform the customer what needs to be resolved and do not proceed with closure.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"}]},"why":"D10: close_debit_card_4721 accepts only ACTIVE or PENDING cards, and this job can meet a FROZEN card. The unfreeze procedure (doc 026) returns it to ACTIVE, so that path is now chained. The refund acknowledgement option from doc 025 is added.","quote":"The debit card must currently be in ACTIVE or PENDING status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"op":"add","list":"steps","after":"check_close_82","item":{"id":"unfreeze_before_close_82","by":"harness","do":"The card must be closed but is FROZEN. Check in get_accounts_82 that the linked checking account is OPEN. Tell the customer the card is reactivated only so it can be closed right away. Unlock unfreeze_debit_card_3893 and call it, then go straight to close_card. If the account is not OPEN or the call returns an error, do not close the card; explain why and follow action_error_82.","call":"call_discoverable_agent_tool","args":{"agent_tool_name":"unfreeze_debit_card_3893","arguments":{"card_id":"the card's card_id from get_cards_82"}},"lookup":["get_cards_82","get_accounts_82","check_close_82"],"after":["check_close_82"],"if":"fraud found, a dispute was filed, the card status is FROZEN, checks 1, 3 and 4 of check_close_82 passed, and the linked checking account is OPEN","quote":"Use unfreeze_debit_card_3893 with the card_id","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026","basis":[{"clause":"closing needs ACTIVE or PENDING","quote":"The debit card must currently be in ACTIVE or PENDING status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"unfreeze needs FROZEN","quote":"Card must currently be in FROZEN status","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"clause":"account OPEN","quote":"The linked checking account must still be OPEN","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"clause":"the result is an active card","quote":"Confirm the card is now active and ready to use immediately","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"}]},"why":"D10: this chains the procedure whose result (an ACTIVE card) meets the close tool's status requirement.","quote":"Use unfreeze_debit_card_3893 with the card_id","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_026"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"close_card","fields":{"after":["unlock_close","unfreeze_before_close_82"],"if":"fraud found, a dispute was filed, check_close_82 passed, and the card is ACTIVE or PENDING (directly, or after unfreeze_before_close_82 succeeded)","basis":[{"clause":"perform the card action after filing","quote":"This parameter records metadata only; the agent must separately perform the indicated card action after filing the dispute.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"},{"clause":"close tool and parameters","quote":"Use close_debit_card_4721 to close the card with parameters: card_id, reason","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"reason fraud_suspected","quote":"Suspected fraud/unauthorized transactions","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_025"},{"clause":"fraud maps to close_and_reissue","quote":"'card_present_fraud' → 'close_and_reissue'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_031"}]},"why":"The condition now includes the check_close_82 result and the unfreeze path. Basis added."},{"op":"add","list":"steps","after":"ask_replacement","item":{"id":"get_user_82","by":"harness","do":"Read the customer's date of birth and address on file for the replacement checks and the mailing address.","call":"get_user_information_by_id","args":{"user_id":"the verified user"},"lookup":[],"after":["ask_replacement"],"if":"the customer wants a replacement","quote":"Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},"why":"check_order_82 needs the age and the US address. This gives it a lookup that reads them (D4).","quote":"Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"check_order_82","fields":{"do":"Check the order rules:
1. The account is OPEN, open at least 3 business days, with a balance of at least $25 (get_accounts_82, time_for_dispute).
2. No ACTIVE and no PENDING card remains on it (get_cards_82, after the closure).
3. The customer is 18 or older and the address is US domestic (get_user_82).
4. Count replacements (issue_reason lost, stolen, fraud, damaged) issued in the last 12 months against the tier limit: Entry 2 (then wait or pay $25), Mid 3 (then wait or pay $15), Premium 5 (then wait), Elite unlimited.
For an Entry-tier account the replacement waits 48 hours after the closure: give the earliest time and do not order now. If a check fails, explain it and do not order.","lookup":["get_accounts_82","get_cards_82","get_user_82","time_for_dispute"],"after":["ask_replacement","get_user_82"],"basis":[{"clause":"account OPEN","quote":"Account status must be OPEN","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"3 business days","quote":"Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"$25 balance","quote":"Account must have a minimum balance of $25 (to cover potential fees)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"one active card","quote":"Customer cannot have more than 1 active debit cards per checking account","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"no pending card","quote":"Customer cannot have a pending debit card order for the same account (check debit_cards table for PENDING status)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"age 18","quote":"Customer must be at least 18 years old (verify using date_of_birth)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"US address","quote":"Customer's address on file must be a valid US domestic address (international shipping is not available)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"what counts as a replacement","quote":"Look for cards with issue_reason of 'lost', 'stolen', 'fraud', or 'damaged'","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Entry limit and fee","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 2-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out of the 12-month window, OR pay a $25 excess replacement fee","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Mid limit and fee","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 3-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out, OR pay a $15 excess replacement fee","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Premium must wait","quote":"If customer has exceeded the 5-card limit, they must wait until oldest replacement ages out (no fee option - must wait)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"Entry 48-hour wait","quote":"48-hour waiting period after card closure before a replacement can be ordered","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"}]},"why":"Doc 023 lists eligibility requirements the old check left out: the 3 business days, the age and the US address. The excess-fee options from doc 029 are added too.","quote":"Account must have been open for at least 3 business days (excluding weekends)","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"op":"change","list":"steps","key":"order_card","fields":{"args":{"agent_tool_name":"order_debit_card_5739","arguments":{"account_id":"the checking account from get_accounts_82","user_id":"the verified user","delivery_option":"STANDARD, EXPEDITED or RUSH, as the customer chose within the tier's options (Entry: STANDARD only)","delivery_fee":"the exact doc 029 tier figure for that option","card_design":"CLASSIC, PREMIUM or CUSTOM, as the customer chose","design_fee":"the exact doc 029 tier figure for that design","shipping_address":"the address the customer confirmed: the address on file from get_user_82, or another US address they give","excess_replacement_fee":"only when over the tier limit and the customer chose to pay: Entry 25, Mid 15; otherwise omit"}},"basis":[{"clause":"exact tier fees","quote":"When using order_debit_card_5739, you must provide the exact delivery_fee and design_fee amounts based on the tier rules below.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_029"},{"clause":"confirmed address","quote":"Confirm the address that the customer would like to mail the card to.","doc":"doc_bank_accounts_bank_accounts_(general)_023"},{"clause":"exc